WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:00.980
MAX SALTONSTALL:
Welcome to BeyondCorp

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:02.810
in a Bottle, where
we explore journeys

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:05.720
into the world of context-aware
access and zero trust networks.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.003
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.370
Slager Bank and Trust,
like many large enterprises

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:15.800
with a long history
of IT infrastructure,

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.570
turned to a perimeter
security model

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:21.290
early on to keep their
corporate resources safe.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:22.370
All the good stuff--

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.310
customer info, company
data, internal applications,

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:26.330
et cetera--

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.530
had to be protected.

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:28.940
So they built walls--

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.220
proxies, firewalls,
and other barriers--

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.080
to keep the public
internet separated

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.120
from their private systems.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:38.050
That left employees with two
options to get work done--

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:41.960
sit in Slager offices
or connect via VPN.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:45.500
They wanted to do better, both
for security and usability.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.630
Having recently learned
about context-aware,

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:49.310
they decided to give it a try.

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:51.260
But how to start?

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.420
To kick it off,
the Slager IT team

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.730
did a broad survey of
their existing systems

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.650
and applications.

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:00.440
They identified Lumen, an
internal marketing analytics

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:04.510
app, as an ideal candidate to
test out context-aware access.

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:07.040
They picked Lumen because
it had a very specific use

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.560
case for a specific set
of people at the company,

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.570
and had few outside
dependencies.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:15.290
It already ran on the web, so
required no platform migration

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:16.430
work.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:19.490
To ensure success, the Slager
team also got leadership buy-in

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:22.710
early on from IT, security,
and marketing teams

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.650
so the top management
knew why they were doing

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:27.200
this and the project timeline.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.300
They explained the benefits
of increased access

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.660
for employees outside the
office and for partner agencies,

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.270
while also addressing risks
of unauthorized access

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:38.060
or application compromise.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:40.820
They began by getting
Lumen running on GCP,

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:43.130
in their case, using
Compute Engine VMs instead

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:45.230
of their on-premise VMs.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.670
Once that was up
and running, they

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.380
could activate
Identity-Aware Proxy

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.570
as part of the
HTTPS load balancer

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:53.190
in front of the cluster.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:56.500
They created simple rules in
IAP to allow the marketing team

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:00.040
to view the web app and the
IT team to manage access.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.780
Then they started
shifting traffic

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.990
from their on-prem instance
of Lumen to the GCP instance,

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:07.540
watching carefully for errors.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.509
The Slager team enjoyed a
couple other side benefits

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:11.830
from this shift.

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:14.530
They got multi-region
availability, reduced latency

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.350
for workers away
from headquarters,

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.910
and they were able to open
up Lumen to specific agency

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:22.120
vendors who had wanted for
years to use the same analytics

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.760
platform to collaborate better
with the internal marketing

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:26.590
teams.

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:29.390
After the successful first step,
the Slager Bank and Trust IT

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:31.900
team had gained both
expertise and confidence

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:34.600
in using GCP and IAP
together and began

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:38.500
to plan future migrations
for other internal services.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:41.200
To get more detail, check out
my blog post, linked below,

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.170
for step-by-step instructions
and subscribe for more videos

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:45.940
on context-aware access.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:48.970
When it comes to protecting your
company, keep your data yours.

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:52.320
[MUSIC PLAYING]

